<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<form name="frmWoD20_1" align="client" theme="dark">
	<scrollBox align="client">
		<!--
			Theme backdrop (SPEC T158). Declared FIRST so it paints behind the boxes, and
			hitTest="false" so it can never eat a click. It carries no field and no
			left/top/width/height: it is not part of the data contract and the gate keeps
			measuring the real boxes for overlap (SPEC V57).

			Hidden here and switched on only by a Victorian theme - and if the art is ever
			missing it simply stays hidden, which is a sheet without an ornament rather than
			a half-painted one (SPEC V56).

			The name carries the tab number because a control name is global across the
			sheet's files: eight tabs sharing one name killed the compile with no message at
			all (SPEC B19 / V59). The Lua matches on the prefix.
		-->
		<image name="themePaper1" align="client" style="stretch" hitTest="false" visible="false"/>

		<!--
			The clan, born ASLEEP (SPEC V173, T432): invisible AND disabled, and no Lua on any
			tab writes the field, so nothing can fill it. It exists now only so the roster of
			CLANS (SPEC I17) has one owner of `clan` the day a round wakes it up - and so V8
			closes, since a widget that is hidden is still a widget.

			Outside every box on purpose: it draws nothing, so it belongs to no layout and it
			cannot push a sibling around. Dimmed like every other read-only widget (SPEC V111)
			- unobservable while it is hidden, but the rule is about what the XML says.

			Sixty entries, the thirteen clans plus the bloodlines the core lists in its tenth
			chapter, with Gargoyles as four rows (SPEC I17). The empty first entry is the one
			every picker carries (SPEC V15).
		-->
		<comboBox name="cboClan" left="0" top="12" width="215" height="25" visible="false" enabled="false" field="clan"/>
		<!--
			Layout grid (SPEC T41, V26, V27). Everything closes on x=1210 / y=784.

			  header  0..1030      EXPERIENCE 1050..1210          y   0..100
			  ATTRIBUTES 0..300    TALENTS 310..600 | SKILLS 615..905 | KNOWLEDGES 920..1210    y 110..450
			  avatar     0..300                                   y 405..760
			                       VIRTUES 310..600               y 460..586
			                       HUMANITY+WILLPOWER 310..600     y 596..760
			                       SPECIALTIES 615..905           y 460..760
			                       HEALTH  920..1210              y 460..766 at ten rows

			Read it as a THREE-COLUMN GRID, which is what V168 measures since the 50th round:
			each box on the bottom row shares both x edges with the column above it - VIRTUES
			and HUMANITY under TALENTS, SPECIALTIES under SKILLS, HEALTH under KNOWLEDGES - the
			last two traded places in the 82nd round, on the user's ask (item 14). The
			49th round had lined up only the two outer ends of the top row; the user asked for
			the other three pairs, and a grid is cheaper to check than four separate rules.

			The columns are 340 tall, not 390: twelve rows from 25 at a pitch of 25 close at
			325, so the old height carried 65px of black tail (SPEC V171). The bottom row rose
			by exactly that 50, and the avatar came with it - it was not in the request, but
			leaving it at 810 would have made it the only thing 50px below everything else.

			HEALTH is the one box that does not end on 760: its height is the ten-row case and
			the renderer shrinks it to the chosen track length (SPEC V49), so at the default of
			seven rows it ends at 685 and only a player who picks ten pushes 6px past the rest.

			Label widths are sized for the LONGER of [en] and [pt]: "Animal Ken" is
			"Empatia com Animais" (19 chars) in pt, so the ability label is 135px, not 80.
			It was 125 until the 49th round, when the ABILITIES frame came off and handed the
			three columns 10px apiece: the point of that request was the names, so the width
			went to the label and the dots moved right with it (SPEC T408, V170).

			Ability / CustomAbility put their first dot at x=135 and Attribute at x=125. V26
			compares rows that are SIBLINGS, and those two never share a box, so each column
			still lines up with itself. Advantages / Willpower carry no label and start at
			x=0 - they live alone in their own box and are centred by the caller.
		-->
		<template name="Header">
			<label left="0" top="5" width="105" height="20" text="$(nome)" horzTextAlign="trailing"/>
			<edit left="112" top="0" width="215" height="25" field="$(field)"/>
		</template>
		<!-- Same row, shorter label. The 105px of `Header` is what `Demeanor` needs in pt
		     ("Comportamento", ~86px) and Demeanor lives in the middle column - keeping that
		     width in the first one is what pushed Nome / Jogador / Cronica to the right.
		     Here the longest pt label is "Jogador", so 75 is room to spare (SPEC V16/V25).
		     V26 compares rows that share a `left`, i.e. rows of the same column, so columns
		     may carry different label widths; all three rows of column one use this one. -->
		<template name="HeaderNarrow">
			<label left="0" top="5" width="75" height="20" text="$(nome)" horzTextAlign="trailing"/>
			<edit left="82" top="0" width="215" height="25" field="$(field)"/>
		</template>
		<template name="HeaderPicker">
			<label left="0" top="5" width="105" height="20" text="$(nome)" horzTextAlign="trailing"/>
			<comboBox left="112" top="0" width="215" height="25" name="cbo$(field)" field="$(field)">
			</comboBox>
		</template>
		<template name="Attribute">
			<label left="0" top="5" width="125" height="20" text="$(nome)"/>
			<image left="125" top="0" width="25" height="25" style="autoFit" src="images/prime_on.png"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="150" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_2" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_2', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="175" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_3" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_3', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="200" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_4" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_4', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="225" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_5" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_5', self);"/>
		</template>
		<!-- Attribute, but dot 1 is a real checkbox instead of a fixed image, so the rating can
		     drop to zero. Only Appearance uses it (SPEC T95). -->
		<template name="AttributeZeroable">
			<label left="0" top="5" width="125" height="20" text="$(nome)"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="125" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_1" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_1', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="150" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_2" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_2', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="175" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_3" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_3', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="200" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_4" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_4', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="225" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_5" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_5', self);"/>
		</template>
		<template name="Ability">
			<label name="dynAbil$(col)$(num)" left="0" top="5" width="135" height="20" text="$(nome)"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="abil$(col)$(num)_1" left="135" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_1" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick(self.abil$(col)$(num)_1.field, self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="abil$(col)$(num)_2" left="160" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_2" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick(self.abil$(col)$(num)_2.field, self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="abil$(col)$(num)_3" left="185" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_3" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick(self.abil$(col)$(num)_3.field, self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="abil$(col)$(num)_4" left="210" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_4" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick(self.abil$(col)$(num)_4.field, self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="abil$(col)$(num)_5" left="235" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_5" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick(self.abil$(col)$(num)_5.field, self);"/>
		</template>
		<!-- Blank rows at the bottom of each ability column, for abilities the book does not list. -->
		<template name="CustomAbility">
			<edit left="0" top="2" width="132" height="21" field="$(field)" fontSize="12"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="135" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_1" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_1', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="160" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_2" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_2', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="185" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_3" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_3', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="210" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_4" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_4', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="235" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_5" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_5', self);"/>
		</template>
		<!-- No label: HUMANITY / WILLPOWER are titled above the track, so "FORCA DE VONTADE"
		     cannot be clipped.

		     The dots start at x=0, not x=125. That 125 origin existed only to line these two
		     tracks up with the 125px row label of Attribute/Ability, back when Virtues and
		     Humanity shared a single box (SPEC B12, T41). T79 split them into separate boxes,
		     so nothing sits to the left of these tracks any more and the offset survived as
		     125px of dead space that pushed the dots against the right edge. The track is now
		     250px wide and the caller centres it with its own left margin. -->
		<template name="Advantages">
			<imageCheckBox left="0" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_1" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_1', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="25" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_2" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_2', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="50" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_3" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_3', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="75" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_4" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_4', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="100" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_5" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_5', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="125" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_6" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_6', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="150" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_7" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_7', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="175" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_8" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_8', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="200" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_9" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_9', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="225" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_10" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_10', self);"/>
		</template>
		<!--
			One health row: level name on the left, damage mark box on the right edge (SPEC T116).

			The mark is NOT a checkBox any more - it holds one of four symbols and cycles on
			click. Emptying a box is healing, so both the wrap and the right-click clear the
			BOTTOM-most marked row, not this one (SPEC V44). The box is a `rectangle`
			with `hitTest="true"` so it takes mouse events, and the `label` inside carries
			`field=` so the NDB renders the stored symbol with no Lua involved - which is also
			what keeps this row and its Combat-tab twin in sync (SPEC V36).

			The level label is 215 wide: the longest pt level is "Ferido Gravemente (-2)"
			(~143px), so it fits with room to spare (SPEC V16 / B17).
		-->
		<template name="HealthRow">
			<label name="dynHealth_$(num)" left="0" top="0" width="215" height="20"/>
			<rectangle left="223" top="0" width="22" height="20" color="#00000000" strokeColor="#FFFFFF" strokeSize="1" xradius="2" yradius="2" hitTest="true" cursor="handPoint" onClick="cycleHealthMark($(num));" onMenu="healHealthMark();">
				<label align="client" field="health_$(num)" horzTextAlign="center" vertTextAlign="center"/>
			</rectangle>
		</template>

		<!--
			One speciality row (SPEC I14, T388): the trait it belongs to, the speciality the
			player types, and a single dot that confirms it.

			The dot's field is `speciality_N_1`, not `speciality_N`, because xpClick splits a
			field into <trait>_<n> to find its rating (SPEC I13): the row is a one-dot trait,
			exactly the shape `background_3` and `background_3_1` already have. The combo owns
			`speciality_N` - the trait NAME, canonical English, which is what the free grant
			writes and what the log reads back (SPEC V147/V152).

			The name starts with `cbo` because that prefix is what the language traversal looks
			for when it translates a picker's items (SPEC V24, WoD20.6), and it carries the row
			number because a control name is global across the sheet's files (SPEC B19/V59).

			Fifty items plus the empty one (SPEC V15): the nine attributes and the forty-one
			abilities, the same names the root form holds in XP_ATTRS and ABILITY_FIELD. The
			gate derives that list from those two tables rather than keeping a copy, so an era
			ability added to one side and not the other is a red gate, not a picker that cannot
			show what Lua wrote (SPEC V148).
		-->
		<template name="SpecialityRow">
			<comboBox name="cboSpeciality$(num)" left="0" top="0" width="150" height="25" field="speciality_$(num)" fontSize="12"/>
			<edit left="155" top="0" width="85" height="25" field="specialityName_$(num)" fontSize="12"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="245" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="speciality_$(num)_1" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('speciality_$(num)_1', self);"/>
		</template>

		<!--
			The last three rows are TYPED, not picked (SPEC I50, V255, user 2026-08-22) - the same
			arrangement the Ghoul tab got in the 85th round: same entry x, same free-text field, same
			dot, and `edt` instead of `cbo` so pickerItems and PICKER_LIST never reach them
			(SPEC V211a, V26).

			The gift a trait hands out stops at the picker rows (SPEC V255d): what locks a granted
			row is the combo's `enabled`, and a typed row has no combo to lock.

			No comment lives INSIDE the template: one there makes rdk -l exit 1 with no message and
			delete the .rpk (SPEC B19, the fifth door, 85th round).
		-->
		<template name="SpecialityFreeRow">
			<edit name="edtSpeciality$(num)" left="0" top="0" width="150" height="25" field="speciality_$(num)" fontSize="12"/>
			<edit left="155" top="0" width="85" height="25" field="specialityName_$(num)" fontSize="12"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="245" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="speciality_$(num)_1" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('speciality_$(num)_1', self);"/>
		</template>

		<template name="Willpower">
			<imageCheckBox left="0" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_1" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_1', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="25" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_2" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_2', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="50" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_3" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_3', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="75" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_4" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_4', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="100" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_5" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_5', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="125" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_6" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_6', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="150" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_7" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_7', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="175" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_8" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_8', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="200" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_9" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_9', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="225" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_10" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_10', self);"/>

			<checkBox left="2" top="20" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_c1"/>
			<checkBox left="27" top="20" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_c2"/>
			<checkBox left="52" top="20" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_c3"/>
			<checkBox left="77" top="20" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_c4"/>
			<checkBox left="102" top="20" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_c5"/>
			<checkBox left="127" top="20" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_c6"/>
			<checkBox left="152" top="20" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_c7"/>
			<checkBox left="177" top="20" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_c8"/>
			<checkBox left="202" top="20" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_c9"/>
			<checkBox left="227" top="20" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_c10"/>
		</template>


		<layout left="0" top="12" width="1030" height="105">
			<rectangle align="client" color="black" xradius="14" yradius="14" cornerType="innerRound"/>

			<layout left="5" top="10" width="297" height="25" >
				<HeaderNarrow field="name" nome="Name"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="320" top="10" width="327" height="25" >
				<HeaderPicker field="nature" nome="Nature"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="698" top="10" width="327" height="25" >
				<Header field="motivation" nome="Motivation"/>
			</layout>

			<layout left="5" top="40" width="297" height="25" >
				<HeaderNarrow field="player" nome="Player"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="320" top="40" width="327" height="25" >
				<HeaderPicker field="demeanor" nome="Demeanor"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="698" top="40" width="327" height="25" >
				<Header field="occupation" nome="Occupation"/>
			</layout>

			<layout left="5" top="70" width="297" height="25" >
				<HeaderNarrow field="chronicle" nome="Chronicle"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="320" top="70" width="327" height="25" >
				<Header field="concept" nome="Concept"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="698" top="70" width="327" height="25" >
				<Header field="residence" nome="Residence"/>
			</layout>
		</layout>

		<layout left="1050" top="12" width="160" height="101">
			<rectangle align="client" color="black" xradius="14" yradius="14" cornerType="innerRound"/>
			<label left="0" top="10" width="160" height="20" text="EXPERIENCE" horzTextAlign="center"/>

			<edit name="edtCurrentXPMain" left="50" top="31" width="60" height="60" fontSize="20" horzTextAlign="center" onUserChange="xpSetCurrent(self, self.edtCurrentXPMain.text);"/>
		</layout>

		<layout left="0" top="127" width="300" height="286">
			<rectangle align="client" color="black" xradius="14" yradius="14" cornerType="innerRound"/>
			<label left="0" top="10" width="300" height="20" text="ATTRIBUTES" horzTextAlign="center"/>

			<label left="-40" top="66" width="100" height="20" text="Physical" horzTextAlign="center" rotationAngle="270"/>

			<layout left="35" top="31" width="250" height="25" >
				<Attribute field="strength" nome="Strength"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="35" top="56" width="250" height="25" >
				<Attribute field="dexterity" nome="Dexterity"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="35" top="81" width="250" height="25" >
				<Attribute field="stamina" nome="Stamina"/>
			</layout>

			<horzLine left="10" top="111" width="280" strokeColor="white"/>

			<label left="-40" top="151" width="100" height="20" text="Social" horzTextAlign="center" rotationAngle="270"/>

			<layout left="35" top="116" width="250" height="25" >
				<Attribute field="charisma" nome="Charisma"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="35" top="141" width="250" height="25" >
				<Attribute field="manipulation" nome="Manipulation"/>
			</layout>
			<!-- Appearance is the one attribute whose first dot can be switched off, by request
			     (SPEC T95). Every other attribute keeps dot 1 as a fixed <image>. Same x for
			     the first dot as the Attribute template, so the column still lines up (V26). -->
			<layout left="35" top="166" width="250" height="25" >
				<AttributeZeroable field="appearance" nome="Appearance"/>
			</layout>

			<horzLine left="10" top="196" width="280" strokeColor="white"/>

			<label left="-40" top="236" width="100" height="20" text="Mental" horzTextAlign="center" rotationAngle="270"/>

			<layout left="35" top="201" width="250" height="25" >
				<Attribute field="perception" nome="Perception"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="35" top="226" width="250" height="25" >
				<Attribute field="inteligence" nome="Intelligence"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="35" top="251" width="250" height="25" >
				<Attribute field="wits" nome="Wits"/>
			</layout>
		</layout>

		<!-- 355 tall, not 405: the preview ends on y=760 with the HUMANITY box, which is
		     where the column closes (SPEC T134, V69). It followed the bottom row up in the
		     50th round - the request did not name it, but a picture reaching 50px below
		     every other box is the ragged edge V69 exists to prevent. -->
		<rectangle left="0" top="417" width="300" height="367" color="DimGray" xradius="5" yradius="5" cornerType="innerRound"/>
		<image left="0" top="417" width="300" height="367" field="avatar" editable="true" style="autoFit"/>

		<!--
			The three ability columns stand loose (SPEC T407, V168, V169). Until the 49th round
			they sat inside one ABILITIES box, whose frame and title spent 30px of width on a
			heading that named what the three titles below it already said. The user asked for
			the heading gone so the names could breathe, so the box the columns were nested in
			is now the row they form: TALENTS starts where VIRTUES starts and KNOWLEDGES closes
			where EXPERIENCE closes. V168 measures it against those two boxes, not against a
			literal, so moving either one without the other turns the gate red.

			Each column still fills black under a centred title of its own width, so V27 and V48
			read them exactly as before. What changed is V40: it now weighs them against every
			box on the tab instead of against the two siblings they shared a frame with - which
			is the check the old nesting was hiding (SPEC B18 is the same lesson from the fill
			side, and the frame that carried that note went out with this comment).

			The gap between columns is 15, the same gap VIRTUES leaves to HEALTH one row down.
		-->
		<layout left="310" top="127" width="290" height="341">
			<rectangle align="client" color="black" xradius="14" yradius="14" cornerType="innerRound"/>
			<label left="0" top="10" width="290" height="20" text="TALENTS" horzTextAlign="center"/>

			<layout left="15" top="31" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="talents" num="1" field="alertness" nome="Alertness"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="56" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="talents" num="2" field="athletics" nome="Athletics"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="81" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="talents" num="3" field="awareness" nome="Awareness"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="106" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="talents" num="4" field="brawl" nome="Brawl"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="131" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="talents" num="5" field="empathy" nome="Empathy"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="156" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="talents" num="6" field="expression" nome="Expression"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="181" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="talents" num="7" field="intimidation" nome="Intimidation"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="206" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="talents" num="8" field="leadership" nome="Leadership"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="231" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="talents" num="9" field="streetwise" nome="Streetwise"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="256" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="talents" num="10" field="subterfuge" nome="Subterfuge"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="281" width="260" height="25" >
				<CustomAbility field="customTalent_1"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="306" width="260" height="25" >
				<CustomAbility field="customTalent_2"/>
			</layout>
		</layout>

		<layout left="615" top="127" width="290" height="341">
			<rectangle align="client" color="black" xradius="14" yradius="14" cornerType="innerRound"/>
			<label left="0" top="10" width="290" height="20" text="SKILLS" horzTextAlign="center"/>

			<layout left="15" top="31" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="skills" num="1" field="animalKen" nome="Animal Ken"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="56" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="skills" num="2" field="crafts" nome="Crafts"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="81" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="skills" num="3" field="etiquette" nome="Etiquette"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="106" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="skills" num="4" field="firearms" nome="Firearms"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="131" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="skills" num="5" field="larceny" nome="Larceny"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="156" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="skills" num="6" field="melee" nome="Melee"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="181" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="skills" num="7" field="performance" nome="Performance"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="206" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="skills" num="8" field="ride" nome="Ride"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="231" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="skills" num="9" field="stealth" nome="Stealth"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="256" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="skills" num="10" field="survival" nome="Survival"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="281" width="260" height="25" >
				<CustomAbility field="customSkill_1"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="306" width="260" height="25" >
				<CustomAbility field="customSkill_2"/>
			</layout>
		</layout>

		<layout left="920" top="127" width="290" height="341">
			<rectangle align="client" color="black" xradius="14" yradius="14" cornerType="innerRound"/>
			<label left="0" top="10" width="290" height="20" text="KNOWLEDGES" horzTextAlign="center"/>

			<layout left="15" top="31" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="knowledges" num="1" field="academics" nome="Academics"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="56" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="knowledges" num="2" field="enigmas" nome="Enigmas"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="81" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="knowledges" num="3" field="finance" nome="Finance"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="106" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="knowledges" num="4" field="investigation" nome="Investigation"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="131" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="knowledges" num="5" field="law" nome="Law"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="156" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="knowledges" num="6" field="medicine" nome="Medicine"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="181" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="knowledges" num="7" field="occult" nome="Occult"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="206" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="knowledges" num="8" field="politics" nome="Politics"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="231" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="knowledges" num="9" field="science" nome="Science"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="256" width="260" height="25" >
				<Ability col="knowledges" num="10" field="technology" nome="Technology"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="281" width="260" height="25" >
				<CustomAbility field="customKnowledge_1"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="15" top="306" width="260" height="25" >
				<CustomAbility field="customKnowledge_2"/>
			</layout>
		</layout>

		<!--
			Bottom row, two columns now, ending at y=760 (SPEC T78/T79, V69):
			  VIRTUES (310-600, y 460-586) over HUMANITY & WILLPOWER (310-600, y 596-760)
			  SPECIALTIES (615-905, y 460-760, SPEC I14) | HEALTH (920-1210)

			Every one of them takes its x from the column above it since the 50th round
			(SPEC V168): Virtues and Humanity from TALENTS, SPECIALTIES from SKILLS, HEALTH
			from KNOWLEDGES. They rose 50 with the same round, which is what the ability
			columns gave back when they stopped carrying a black tail (SPEC V171).

			Virtues and Humanity are 290 wide, not 410: their content is a 250px track (a 125px
			label plus 5 dots, or 10 bare dots), so 410 left a wide empty margin and made the
			Humanity/Willpower dots read as right-aligned. 290 = 250 + a 20px margin each side,
			which centres both tracks. The 120px freed went to HEALTH.

			HEALTH is 290 wide because 150 was not enough for its own labels: "Wounded (-2)" is
			"Ferido Gravemente (-2)" in pt, ~143px in a 125px checkBox. V16 only measures
			<label>, never <checkBox>, so that overflow was never flagged by the gate.

			Faith is gone from this tab on purpose: `faith_1`..`_5` are now the dots of the
			TRUE FAITH row on the Powers tab, so a saved sheet keeps its rating (SPEC V35).
		-->
		<layout left="310" top="478" width="290" height="128">
			<rectangle align="client" color="black" xradius="14" yradius="14" cornerType="innerRound"/>
			<label left="0" top="10" width="290" height="20" text="VIRTUES" horzTextAlign="center"/>

			<layout left="20" top="35" width="250" height="25" >
				<Attribute field="conscience" nome="Conscience"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="20" top="64" width="250" height="25" >
				<Attribute field="selfControl" nome="Self-Control"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="20" top="93" width="250" height="25" >
				<Attribute field="courage" nome="Courage"/>
			</layout>
		</layout>

		<layout left="310" top="624" width="290" height="160">
			<rectangle align="client" color="black" xradius="14" yradius="14" cornerType="innerRound"/>

			<label left="0" top="10" width="290" height="20" text="HUMANITY" horzTextAlign="center"/>
			<layout left="20" top="35" width="250" height="25" >
				<Advantages field="humanity"/>
			</layout>

			<label left="0" top="80" width="290" height="20" text="WILLPOWER" horzTextAlign="center"/>
			<layout left="20" top="105" width="250" height="45" >
				<Willpower field="willpower"/>
			</layout>
		</layout>

		<!--
			HEALTH is positional now (SPEC T96): row N is the Nth damage box, `health_1`..`_10`.
			The old semantic names (bruised/hurt/injured/...) are gone - they could not express a
			track where the label repeats (four "Bruised" rows at 10 levels), so they are declared
			orphans in SPEC I3 and a sheet saved before this loses its health marks. Requested.

			The labels carry NO text= here: renderHealthTrack() on the root form writes them from
			HEALTH_LEVELS, already translated, and hides the rows past the chosen length. The
			`dyn` name prefix is what keeps the WoD20.6 language traversal off them - it snapshots
			authored English once, and would restore a stale label after a length change (V31).

			Each row is a named layout so the renderer can hide label and mark box together; the
			mark itself is a four-symbol box, see the HealthRow template (SPEC T116).

			height=306 is the TEN-row case on purpose (SPEC V49): the renderer shrinks the box to
			fit the chosen track length, so the file always declares the tallest it can ever be
			and the box-overlap check (V40), which reads this file and not the running sheet,
			keeps measuring the worst case.

			Title is 205 wide, not 280, to leave room for the level combo. That is under the 80%
			the gate treats as a full-width section title, so V27 still holds for this box.
			245px per row because "Wounded (-2)" is "Ferido Gravemente (-2)" in pt (V38 / B17).
		-->
		<layout name="dynHealth_box" left="920" top="478" width="290" height="307">
			<rectangle align="client" color="black" xradius="14" yradius="14" cornerType="innerRound"/>
			<!-- How long the track is moved to the storyteller's box in the 82nd round (SPEC I35,
			     V234): it was never the player's call, and it was the last thing on this sheet
			     held by two widgets on one field. The title spans the whole box now that it no
			     longer shares the row with a combo, so horzTextAlign centres it on the BOX. -->
			<label left="0" top="10" width="290" height="20" text="HEALTH" horzTextAlign="center"/>

			<layout name="dynHealth_row1" left="22" top="34" width="246" height="20"><HealthRow num="1"/></layout>
			<layout name="dynHealth_row2" left="22" top="61" width="246" height="20"><HealthRow num="2"/></layout>
			<layout name="dynHealth_row3" left="22" top="88" width="246" height="20"><HealthRow num="3"/></layout>
			<layout name="dynHealth_row4" left="22" top="115" width="246" height="20"><HealthRow num="4"/></layout>
			<layout name="dynHealth_row5" left="22" top="142" width="246" height="20"><HealthRow num="5"/></layout>
			<layout name="dynHealth_row6" left="22" top="169" width="246" height="20"><HealthRow num="6"/></layout>
			<layout name="dynHealth_row7" left="22" top="196" width="246" height="20"><HealthRow num="7"/></layout>
			<layout name="dynHealth_row8" left="22" top="223" width="246" height="20"><HealthRow num="8"/></layout>
			<layout name="dynHealth_row9" left="22" top="250" width="246" height="20"><HealthRow num="9"/></layout>
			<layout name="dynHealth_row10" left="22" top="277" width="246" height="20"><HealthRow num="10"/></layout>
		</layout>

		<!--
			SPECIALTIES (SPEC I14, T388) took the corner the 46th round emptied when BACKGROUNDS
			moved to the Traits tab. Since the 50th it has no coordinates of its own: it takes
			both x edges from KNOWLEDGES above it and closes on the bottom line with the rest of
			the row (SPEC V146, V168, V69).

			Nine rows: the first at 25 and a pitch of 30 puts the ninth at 265..290, and a tenth
			would want 295..320 in a box that is 300 tall. Nine is what fits, and a table with no
			free slot says so with a pop-up rather than dropping the grant (SPEC V146/V153).

			No column headings: the box has one title and the three columns explain themselves.
			The row is 270 wide inside a 290 box - 150 for the trait, 85 for the text, 25 for the
			dot, 5 between each. It was 300 in a 320 box until the 50th round narrowed the box to
			match KNOWLEDGES; the 30 came out of the free-text field and not out of the picker,
			which has to show "Empatia com Animais" at 19 characters (SPEC V16).
		-->
		<layout left="615" top="478" width="290" height="306">
			<rectangle align="client" color="black" xradius="14" yradius="14" cornerType="innerRound"/>
			<label left="0" top="10" width="290" height="20" text="SPECIALTIES" horzTextAlign="center"/>

			<layout left="10" top="31" width="270" height="25"><SpecialityRow num="1"/></layout>
			<layout left="10" top="61" width="270" height="25"><SpecialityRow num="2"/></layout>
			<layout left="10" top="91" width="270" height="25"><SpecialityRow num="3"/></layout>
			<layout left="10" top="121" width="270" height="25"><SpecialityRow num="4"/></layout>
			<layout left="10" top="151" width="270" height="25"><SpecialityRow num="5"/></layout>
			<layout left="10" top="181" width="270" height="25"><SpecialityRow num="6"/></layout>
			<layout left="10" top="211" width="270" height="25"><SpecialityFreeRow num="7"/></layout>
			<layout left="10" top="241" width="270" height="25"><SpecialityFreeRow num="8"/></layout>
			<layout left="10" top="271" width="270" height="25"><SpecialityFreeRow num="9"/></layout>
		</layout>

	</scrollBox>

	<!--
		The health labels are written by Lua, so they need re-rendering whenever the track length
		or the language changes. Two independent entry points on purpose (SPEC V19 / V33): the
		dataLink covers later edits, onNodeReady covers the sheet simply being opened.
	-->
	<dataLink fields="{'healthLevels', 'language'}" onChange="renderHealthTrack(self, 'dynHealth_');"/>

	<!-- The experience box is worked out, not stored (SPEC I11): it follows the one saved
	     number, and every dot on this tab redraws it through the guard. -->
	<dataLink field="xpTotal" onChange="renderXPBoxes(self);"/>

	<!-- A free speciality is locked (SPEC V161/V164), and which rows are free is written in
	     the stamps. Watching them covers the grant that happened on ANOTHER client at the
	     table: the field arrives over the NDB, and the row locks here too.

	     `xpFree` carries no widget by design - it is Lua-owned, the declared exception to
	     V8 (SPEC I3, B25). -->
	<dataLink field="xpFree" onChange="renderSpecialities(self);"/>

	<event name="onShow">
		wodTrace("WoD20.1.onShow");
		renderXPBoxes(self);
	</event>

	<event name="onNodeReady">
		renderHealthTrack(self, 'dynHealth_');
		renderXPBoxes(self);
		renderSpecialities(self);
	</event>
</form>
